dsh-turn-dial README · How it works：1. reads the list height the virtualiser writes on the marks container to learn the real turn count, then grows the scroll box to that height, which makes the virtualiser mount every mark;
2. rotates each mark about a hub on the dial's right edge and pushes it out to the dial radius, so a mark becomes a radial graduation;
3. draws the graduations with CSS on the marks themselves and the face with one SVG layered under the pointer events;
4. rotates the needle with a single inline transform whenever the current turn changes.
